      },
      "rev_n_1_f05e69_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_f05e69_0",
        "node_id": "n_1_f05e69",
        "thought_text": "Calculate the shortest path between X and Y without considering any SWERC-owned banks. This will give us the baseline cost against which we can compare the cost when using SWERC's banks. If the baseline cost is already the minimum, then the answer is 'Impossible'.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794410087.8354099
      },
      "rev_n_2_a224bf_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_a224bf_0",
        "node_id": "n_2_a224bf",
        "thought_text": "For each possible fee value, starting from the highest possible (which would be the maximum fee among all partnerships), calculate the shortest path between X and Y using only SWERC-owned banks. If at any point, the cost of this path becomes less than or equal to the baseline cost, then that fee value is the largest possible fee.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794410087.8354182
      },
      "rev_n_3_837252_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_837252_0",
        "node_id": "n_3_837252",
        "thought_text": "Check if there exists a path between X and Y that does not involve any SWERC-owned banks. If such a path exists and its cost is less than the cost of any path involving SWERC-owned banks, then the answer is 'Impossible'. Otherwise, the answer could potentially be 'Infinity' if SWERC can always find a cheaper path regardless of the fee.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794410087.835422
      },
      "rev_n_4_d4712c_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_4_d4712c_0",
        "node_id": "n_4_d4712c",
        "thought_text": "Re-evaluate the condition for checking if SWERC can provide the cheapest way to transfer money between X and Y. Instead of comparing the cost of the path using SWERC-owned banks with the baseline cost directly, consider the difference between the two costs. If the difference is positive, SWERC can provide a cheaper path.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "3771473033298352877",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794410199.8575091
      },
      "rev_n_5_93a835_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_5_93a835_0",
        "node_id": "n_5_93a835",
        "thought_text": "Implement a binary search on the fee values in reverse order, starting from the highest possible fee (maximum fee among all partnerships) down to 1. This approach ensures that we find the largest fee where SWERC can still provide the cheapest path between X and Y.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "3771473033298352877",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794410199.85752
      },
      "rev_n_6_94ee31_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_6_94ee31_0",
        "node_id": "n_6_94ee31",
        "thought_text": "Optimize the Dijkstra algorithm to handle the case where the maximum fee is set to infinity. This will allow us to compute the baseline cost efficiently without modifying the graph structure.",
